// Test: bugfixes/validator_custom_takes_a_handler
// Grammar: function_call (validator.custom)
// Semantic: SEM001 — `validator.custom(v, fn)` takes a `handler`: a
//   reference to the check function `boolean fn(string value)` (developer
//   decision)
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.184
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   error[SEM001]
//   Cannot unify types: integer and handler
//
// Guards the decision: before the §15 declarations validator.custom took an
// `any`, so an integer passed as the check function compiled and the run
// called whatever function table slot it named.

start:
	integer v = validator.field(validator.create(), "code")
	v = validator.custom(v, 5)
	print(validator.isOk(validator.run(v, 0)))
